 "about": "The execution lease's runtime files, read by both lease.mjs (js) and the launcher's lease-check (rust). A tombstone's value, or null when refused; a record accepted or not. Rust is never more lenient than JS: where they differ (16-digit tombstones are never written by lease.mjs; 5.0 and duplicate keys, lg's or gen's, are never written by its JSON.stringify), Rust refuses, which fails closed. Records carry sg, the suspend gate's generation (lease-on r1.5 \u00a76.2), a safe integer >= 0. The gate rows decide the suspend gate (\u00a76.1) from the two files' texts (null = absent) and now on CLOCK_BOOTTIME (ms): open is the generation, or null when closed; JS and Rust must agree exactly.",
